course: dictionary
lesson: 6067
title: Words from farm and wool
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A merino is a kind of sheep with very fine, soft wool. The word can also mean the wool itself, or cloth made from it. Read the words around it to work out which meaning fits: «a merino jumper» is clothing, so merino means wool or cloth there.
explain: Look at this context: «Most farm sheep grow wool that never stops, so they must be shorn at least once a year, while wild sheep shed their coats every spring; an Australian merino that escaped shearing for years carried about 41 kilograms of fleece.» Shorn means had its wool cut off. Fleece is the wool a sheep grows. The clues tell you what the words mean even when you have not met them before.
explain: Merino sheep first came from Spain and are now raised in large numbers in Australia and New Zealand. In geography, that makes them part of farming history and trade. Phrases like «merino wool» and «merino sheep» show you which meaning is used: the wool, or the animal.
fact: A merino is a breed of sheep with very fine, soft wool.
fact: Merino wool is the soft, warm wool from these sheep, or cloth made from it.
fact: Merino sheep first came from Spain and are now raised in large numbers in Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Shorn» means had its wool cut off, as when a farmer shears a sheep.
fact: Merino jumpers, socks and base layers keep you warm without itching.
exercise: In «a merino jumper», what is merino? | A big dog | A farm building | A cold, wet day | *Soft wool or cloth made from it
exercise: Merino sheep first came from which country? | *Spain | Australia | New Zealand | England
exercise: «They must be shorn at least once a year.» What does shorn mean here? | *Had its wool cut off | Painted blue | Washed in a river | Fed with grass
test: «The merino jumper kept her warm all winter without any itching.» What is a merino jumper made from? | *Soft wool or cloth from merino sheep | Metal wire | Rubber | Paper
test: In the lesson sentence, what does «fleece» mean? | A kind of sandwich | A type of fish | Food for sheep | *The wool a sheep grows
exam: Which phrase names the wool rather than the animal? | *merino wool | a merino flock | merino sheep | merino farmers
